  "alt": "Three difficulty tiers for beta reduction. A direct application reaches its normal form in one substitution. A chained application takes two steps, keeping its bindings, before it reaches a normal form. The Omega combinator reduces to itself forever, so the correct answer is to detect that it has no normal form rather than invent a terminating one.",
  "caption": "Tier 3 separates systems that preserve fixed-point semantics from systems that write a tidy answer for Ω.",
